  "summary": "All checks pass (lint, build, 145 tests).\n\n**What I changed here**\n\n1. **Concurrent redline conflict (UC5)** — the `useSubmitReview` hook (which already detects the backend's 409) had no UI consumer. Added `src/features/negotiation/components/RedlineSubmitPanel.jsx` and mounted it on `NegotiationTrackerPage` for reviewers/owners while the negotiation isn't Agreed. A successful submit clears the box and reports the new version; a 409 renders \"A newer version was submitted while you were editing. Please refresh and reapply your changes.\" with a Refresh action that refetches the tracker. Keeping *both* versions on conflict is backend behaviour — left to that side.\n\n2. **Mandatory clause can't be removed (UC3)** — `ClauseDetailDrawer` now blocks the Reject (remove) action when `clause.isMandatory` and shows \"This clause is mandatory and cannot be removed from the contract.\"; optional clauses reject as before.\n\n3. **Audit log immutability (UC11)** — no edit/delete affordance existed, but the rule wasn't stated. Added the notice \"Audit log entries cannot be modified or deleted.\" to the Settings `AuditLogTab` and to the clause-analysis `AuditLogViewer`. API- and database-level enforcement belongs to the backend repository.\n\nReading taken: the smaller one — each item is a message/guard on the existing screens, not a new feature area.",
